# 402 Agent for Pump.fun Deployment (Solana Native)

A payment-gated API service that enables AI agents to deploy tokens on Pump.fun using the HTTP 402 (Payment Required) standard with native Solana (SOL/USDC) payments.

## Overview

This agent implements the 402 payment protocol with Solana blockchain payments, allowing AI agents and automated systems to programmatically deploy tokens on Pump.fun by paying per request in SOL or USDC. The service acts as a bridge between payment verification and Pump.fun's deployment API.

## Features

- **402 Payment Protocol**: Standard HTTP 402 response with Solana payment address
- **Native Solana Payments**: SOL and SPL token (USDC) support
- **Pump.fun Integration**: Direct token deployment to Solana via Pump.fun
- **Agent-Friendly API**: RESTful endpoints designed for AI agent consumption
- **Real-time Payment Verification**: WebSocket monitoring of Solana transactions
- **Escrow Protection**: Optional escrow for failed deployments
- **Rate Limiting**: Configurable limits per payment tier
- **Webhook Support**: Real-time deployment status updates

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────┐    402 Request      ┌──────────────┐
│  AI Agent   │ ──────────────────> │  402 Agent   │
│   Wallet    │                     │   Service    │
│             │ <────────────────── │              │
└──────┬──────┘  Payment Address    └──────┬───────┘
       │                                    │
       │  Send SOL/USDC                     │ Monitor
       │                                    │ Payment
       v                                    v
┌─────────────┐                      ┌──────────────┐
│   Solana    │ ──────────────────> │   Pump.fun   │
│ Blockchain  │   Deploy Token       │     API      │
└─────────────┘                      └──────────────┘
```

## Installation

### Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+
- Solana wallet with SOL for gas fees
- Solana RPC endpoint (Helius, QuickNode, or self-hosted)
- Pump.fun API access
- PostgreSQL or MongoDB for payment tracking

### Setup

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/pumpfun-402-solana-agent.git
cd pumpfun-402-solana-agent

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Copy environment template
cp .env.example .env

# Configure your environment variables
nano .env
```

### Environment Variables

```env
# Solana Configuration
